Here's TUnit's lifecycle at each scope:

---

### 1. Before/after every test in a class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public async Task ResetDatabase(TestContext context)
    {
        await InMemoryDb.ResetAsync();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public async Task Cleanup(TestContext context)
    {
        // optional per-test teardown
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Order_WithNoItems_Throws() { /* ... */ }
}
```

---

### 2. Once before first / after last test in a class (class-scoped fixture)

```csharp
public class CustomerApiTests
{
    [Before(Class)]
    public static async Task OpenFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once before the first test in this class
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static async Task DisposeFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once after the last test in this class
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task GetCustomer_ReturnsOk() { /* ... */ }
}
```

> Note: class-level hooks must be **static**.

---

### 3. Once before/after all tests in the assembly

```csharp
public class WireMockSetup
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StartWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // start in-process WireMock server
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StopWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // stop server
    }
}
```

---

### 4. Once at the very start/end of the entire test session

```csharp
public class GlobalDatabaseSetup
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static async Task ApplyMigrations(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await Db.MigrateAsync();
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static async Task TearDown(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await Db.DropAsync();
    }
}
```

---

### Quick-reference table

| Scope | Before | After |
|-------|--------|-------|
| Each test | `[Before(Test)]` | `[After(Test)]` |
| Class (once) | `[Before(Class)]` (static) | `[After(Class)]` (static) |
| Assembly (once) | `[Before(Assembly)]` (static) | `[After(Assembly)]` (static) |
| Session (once) | `[Before(TestSession)]` (static) | `[After(TestSession)]` (static) |

**Bonus:** `[BeforeEvery(Test)]` / `[AfterEvery(Test)]` are *global* hooks that fire for every test across the entire run (useful for cross-cutting concerns like logging), regardless of which class the test lives in. The same `Every` variant exists for `Class` and `Assembly`.

All hooks can be `async Task` and optionally accept a `CancellationToken` as a second parameter.
